# paradigm-threat-files: git remotes (single `main`)

**Canon:** [`docs/GIT_REMOTE_STRATEGY.md`](docs/GIT_REMOTE_STRATEGY.md)

## Rules (compact)

- **One tip:** GitLab **`main`** and Relay **`dfw1` / `hkg1` / `lon1` `main`** stay identical.
- **Forge SoT:** remote **`gitlab`**, branch **`main`**.
- **Local default checkout:** branch **`main`**.
- **Ordinary commit + push:** `git push gitlab HEAD:main`.
- **Go live / push remotes / push everything live:** push the **same** tip to all three Relay `main`, then confirm GitLab matches.
- **Never** dual cherry-pick as sync. **Never** force-push Relay `main` unless the author explicitly orders it (prefer reclone from GitLab).
- **Never** land long-lived commits on only one Relay.
- Do **not** use retired workarounds: `gitlab` work branch, `relay-publish`.
- **Media:** real binaries at public paths; **`assets.manifest.json`** is the IPFS index. Never commit `relay-ipfs-v1` text as `.png`/`.jpg`/etc. Canon: [`docs/MEDIA_AND_IPFS.md`](docs/MEDIA_AND_IPFS.md).
